course: dictionary
lesson: 5029
title: Inhale and breathe in
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To inhale means to breathe air into your lungs. Breathe in means the same thing, so when you are told to inhale deeply, take a big, slow breath in.
explain: «Inhaled steroids are not the same as the steroids some athletes misuse.» The word inhaled tells you the medicine was breathed in, not swallowed. The clue is in the word itself, so check it against what you know: you can only breathe in something through your nose or mouth.
explain: Inhale is the opposite of exhale. In science lessons you inhale oxygen and exhale carbon dioxide. When you meet a new word, ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
fact: Inhale means to breathe air or another gas into your lungs.
fact: Inhale can also mean to breathe in smoke, dust or medicine.
fact: Informal: inhale can mean to eat something very fast, as if breathing it in.
fact: Children with asthma use an inhaler to inhale medicine.
fact: In safety, you should never inhale smoke, fumes or dust.
exercise: «Take a deep breath and inhale slowly.» What does inhale mean here? | Shout very loudly | Breathe air out of your lungs | Hold your breath under water | *Breathe air into your lungs
exercise: In science you inhale oxygen and exhale carbon dioxide. Which word means the opposite of inhale? | *Exhale | Swallow | Stretch | Blow
exercise: Safety rules say you should not inhale smoke, fumes or dust. Why? | They make your hair grow | *They can harm your lungs | They taste sweet | They make you taller
test: «Children with asthma use an inhaler to inhale their medicine.» What does inhale mean in this sentence? | To swallow a pill | *To breathe in medicine | To drink water | To rub cream on the skin
test: Which phrase means the same as «inhale deeply»? | Blow out the candles | *Breathe in slowly and fully | Hold your nose | Stop breathing
exam: Which meaning of inhale is informal? | Breathe out slowly | Breathe medicine in through an inhaler | Breathe air into your lungs | *Eat something very fast, as if breathing it in
